{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791760007,"nonce":"8xQRtWlbB7No+9r7tPFquiBA2k8=","title":"Spend cap reserves a flat 0.002 USD per batch job regardless of model","message":"Found in spec 020 review. screen.ESTIMATED_COST_PER_REQUEST_USD (0.002) caps submit_batch at floor(remaining/0.002) and _pending_batch_usd counts uncollected batches at 0.002, whatever the model and even with measured history; rescore.cost_per_job falls back to 0.002 with no history; the Anthropic branch of rescore._execute submits without checking plan.max_usd. A screen_scorer priced above that (e.g. anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5, about 0.0051/job batched) lets the nightly run and confirmed re-scores overrun the daily cap about 2.5x (cap 2 USD, billed about 5). Fix: reserve max(0.002, measured mean, table price at backfill.TYPICAL_USAGE) per model in submit_batch, _pending_batch_usd (store per-batch reservation) and cost_per_job; make the Anthropic re-score batch cut its limit to plan.max_usd / per_job. Tests: Sonnet 5.5 screening never submits more than the cap covers at its table price; re-score never exceeds max_usd.","files":null}]}